Collard, the Wilkies, Challenger, Seymour, all tuned the meantone temperament, except that like Arnold Schlick, 1511 (see p. 546d), they raised the *G*♯ somewhat to mitigate the 'wolf' resulting from the Fifth *E*♭ : *G*♯ in place of *E*♭ : *A*♭. Hence Mr. James @@R1@@
