gives the proper figures for equal temperament, shews how it arose, that its Fifths are too flat and its major Thirds too sharp, adding 'this will render all keys equally imperfect,' but says nothing to recommend it. Yet in 1840 Dr. Crotch (who died in 1847) had his @@R1@@
